{"parentUuid":"e0aab741-cfb2-4c19-878b-c0ab359e4be2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c0df9cdd-fb09-443f-b1d3-66402e708236","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Cj9XBJu2UwSaE8WvNEX7D","type":"tool_result","content":"ActionAdded A1"}]},"uuid":"20c0d468-775a-4310-8506-6e7e9506470d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:41:48.243Z","toolUseResult":"ActionAdded A1","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e0aab741-cfb2-4c19-878b-c0ab359e4be2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/tmp/zg-eval","sessionId":"f203c932-501d-406b-bbb8-16278dbec18e","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"4132db9d-755f-456c-ba70-80585873e3be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgJ5iSFZAGm66cL8cL3we","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Goal opened: plan the March team offsite. The venue booking before Friday is tracked as action A1, owned by you.\n\n**Decide first: the exact dates and the headcount.** Everything else in the plan hangs off those two, and the venue offer is only bookable once you can commit to them. Settle both before Friday, then book.\n\nDecide in this order:\n\n1. **Dates.** Pick the March days now. Check them against the team's calendars, school holidays in Sweden, and any release or quarter-end commitments. If the venue offer is tied to specific dates, that narrows this to a yes or no.\n2. **Headcount and who.** Confirm whether it is the core team only or includes contractors, partners, or leadership guests. The number drives room capacity, catering, and cost.\n3. **Budget ceiling.** You need this only to the point of knowing the venue fits. Travel, food, and activities can be refined after the booking.\n4. **Purpose and format.** Strategy, team building, or working sessions. This matters for the room layout and breakout needs you tell the venue, but it can be a rough answer this week.\n\nOnce the venue is booked, the remaining planning is agenda, travel logistics, catering, activities, and communication to the team, none of which is time-critical this week.\n\nWhat I need from you to go further:\n\n- The March dates you are considering, or the dates the venue offer is tied to\n- Expected headcount\n- The venue name and what the offer covers\n- Rough budget\n\nYour Google Calendar and Gmail connectors are not authorized in this session. If you want me to check team availability or read the venue's offer email, authorize them in your claude.ai connector settings."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":30639,"output_tokens":529,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":30639,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgJ5iRsz7AYYUyoPnw7SM","requestRef":"9cb47967-9218-462b-aaa9-7aed35c6fe38","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-1","attributionSkill":"zg:open","attributionPlugin":"zg","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ce3acca-1a12-423a-9a62-9fc4ae17a9b4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:41:59.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/tmp/zg-eval","sessionId":"f203c932-501d-406b-bbb8-16278dbec18e","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"82080df1-71eb-42dd-b94c-db62b1ae8b00","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35cc92da-aa79-4992-8fae-488fc2722593","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<command-message>zg:close</command-message>\n<command-name>/zg:close</command-name>\n<command-args>Cancel it, and the venue too. I'd rather not say why.</command-args>"},"uuid":"f1b7d432-582f-402a-a6c2-696209b83ef6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:42:05.021Z","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":2},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/tmp/zg-eval","sessionId":"f203c932-501d-406b-bbb8-16278dbec18e","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"f1b7d432-582f-402a-a6c2-696209b83ef6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35cc92da-aa79-4992-8fae-488fc2722593","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The human is closing this zg session. Cancel it, and the venue too. I'd rather not say why.\n\n1. Ask everything in one question dialog of up to 4 questions: the goal's\n   outcome (achieved, failed or cancelled, unless they just said) and each\n   open action's (done, cancelled, or to be filed). More open items go in\n   further dialogs, asked back to back. Each question's options are only\n   those three, each with a preview of what zg records for that pick (e.g.\n   `failed`, nothing more); the preview is what lets them press n to add a\n   note.\n2. Record them all: each action with mcp__zg__action (export lists it in the\n   handoff), and the goal with mcp__zg__close_goal as its description says.\n   The reason is whatever words they gave about how it ended, verbatim, even\n   short or explaining nothing (\"drop it\", \"I'd rather not say why\"): a note\n   on a pick is the reason, with source dialog; words they typed in chat are\n   the reason, with source chat. Only a bare pick has none: it records source\n   dialog and no reason, except a bare pick of failed: before recording the\n   goal, ask why in chat and record their answer as the reason, with source\n   chat. Their words are any reason, never an option's label or description.\n3. Then write the handoff with mcp__zg__handoff right away, also when the\n   goal failed or was cancelled, without asking first: the next session's one\n   goal (after such an end it can be a conversation about what to do\n   instead), the decisions it must respect (lasting or not), and the few\n   references it needs. Write it as they'll paste it, their message to the\n   next session: \"I\" is them, \"you\" is Claude. Show what it returns verbatim;\n   when they want changes, write it again.\n"}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"468dbe97-7821-4206-9b72-e3c38993b77d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:42:05.021Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/tmp/zg-eval","sessionId":"f203c932-501d-406b-bbb8-16278dbec18e","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
